WSI/X11: wait for rendering before presenting when nothing else syncs.

Without DRI3/Present 1.4 explicit sync, the X11 WSI attaches the render fence
to the dma-buf through DMA_BUF_IOCTL_IMPORT_SYNC_FILE and lets the X server
wait implicitly. Kernels without that ioctl (the Note10+'s 4.14, the S20's
4.19) get no dma_buf_semaphore, and Turnip's KGSL backend attaches no
implicit fences, so in FIFO and IMMEDIATE mode xcb_present_pixmap went out
while Adreno was still resolving bins. Termux:X11 and mutter then showed
partly rendered frames: horizontal splits with tile steps, and black or
see-through rectangles in ARGB windows.

The present thread already waits on the image's fence for MAILBOX. Do the
same whenever the swapchain has neither explicit sync nor a dma-buf
semaphore. Software WSI already waits in wsi_common_queue_present.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c	2026-11-18 23:41:45.968415968 -0800
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c	2026-11-18 23:41:45.992416086 -0800
@@ -2524,9 +2524,17 @@
 
       VkPresentModeKHR present_mode = chain->images[image_index].present_mode;
 
-      /* Not necessary to block when we have explicit sync */
+      /* Not necessary to block when we have explicit sync.  Without explicit
+       * sync and without a dma-buf semaphore, the X server only waits for
+       * rendering if the kernel driver attaches implicit fences to the
+       * dma-buf.  KGSL does not, and kernels without
+       * DMA_BUF_IOCTL_IMPORT_SYNC_FILE cannot attach one for us, so the
+       * server would read a partly rendered image.  Wait on the CPU instead.
+       */
       bool need_fence_wait =
-            x11_needs_wait_for_fences(chain->base.wsi, wsi_conn, present_mode) &&
+            (x11_needs_wait_for_fences(chain->base.wsi, wsi_conn, present_mode) ||
+             (!chain->base.wsi->sw &&
+              chain->base.dma_buf_semaphore == VK_NULL_HANDLE)) &&
             !chain->base.image_info.explicit_sync;
 
       bool need_timing_fence_wait = x11_swapchain_present_timing_is_out_of_order_completion(
